# Traffic Sign Recognition using CNN

A university project developed in 2023 at Rzeszów University of Technology, focused on recognizing road traffic signs using a Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) implemented in Python.

## Technologies

- Python
- TensorFlow / Keras
- OpenCV
- NumPy
- Pandas
- Scikit-learn

## Project Description

The application uses a CNN model to classify 43 categories of traffic signs based on the German Traffic Sign Recognition Benchmark (GTSRB) dataset.

The project includes:

- Image preprocessing (grayscale conversion, histogram equalization and normalization)
- Training a convolutional neural network
- Data augmentation
- Model evaluation
- Traffic sign recognition using a webcam

## Project Files

- `training.py` — model training and evaluation
- `test.py` — traffic sign recognition using a webcam
- `my_model.h5` — saved neural network model
- `DaneBadawcze/` — image dataset
- `EtykietyDanych.csv` — traffic sign labels
- `PROJEKT-PYTHON.pdf` — project documentation (in Polish)

## Running the Project

The project was developed in 2023 using an older Python and Keras environment. Some dependencies may require compatible versions.

Install the required dependencies:

```bash
pip install -r requirements
```

To run the webcam recognition application:

```bash
python test.py
```

A working webcam and a compatible Python environment are required.

To retrain the model:

```bash
python training.py
```

